    "narrative": "The core of LawDog\u2019s production today hinges on a trio of high-floor anchors: **Lawrence Butler** (73.47), **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47), and **Bryce Harper** (70.02). **Lawrence Butler** sits at the top of our rankings, benefitting from an elite leadoff spot against a mediocre arm, while **Jonathan Aranda**\u2019s score is buoyed by an exceptional park factor and a favorable platoon advantage. **Bryce Harper** continues to provide steady output in the 3-hole despite the moderate matchup against a left-handed pitcher, showing elite stability in his xwOBA metrics. We are also leaning heavily on **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.82), both of whom take advantage of positive park factors and high-leverage spots in the batting order to provide consistent value above the 60-point threshold.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (45.35), whose speed-heavy profile is always tempting in our category-weighted strategy. While his projected efficiency nearly cracked the starting rotation, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a tough draw against a quality left-handed starter and the superior situational scores of **Gavin Sheets** and **JJ Bleday**. Risk management remains a primary focus, as we have several \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Daulton Varsho**. If official lineups cause significant demotions in the batting order for these players, we must remain prepared to swap in secondary options. We continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith**, who remains sidelined on the IL, as we preserve our limited game caps for high-efficiency matchups.",
